{
  "answer_markdown": "Yes, Mistral models support a **moderations feature** through dedicated moderation models. Specifically:

- The **[Mistral Moderation](https://docs.mistral.ai/models/mistral-moderation-24-11)** model (`mistral-moderation-2411`) provides a **moderations** endpoint to classify and detect harmful text content [8].

- The **[Mistral Moderation 2](https://docs.mistral.ai/models/mistral-moderation-26-03)** model (`mistral-moderation-2603`) is an improved version with enhanced features, including **moderations** and **chat moderations** (for multi-turn conversations), along with jailbreaking detection [3][4][8].

These models can be used via:
1. **Custom Guardrails** (declared directly in API requests for chat completions, conversations, or agent-level configuration) [1][5].
2. **Moderation API** (dedicated endpoint for classifying text across policy categories, with raw scores and full control) [1][5].

Example API calls for moderation are provided in the documentation:

- **Moderations (text classification):**
  ```curl
  curl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/moderations \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $MISTRAL_API_KEY" \
    -d '{
      "model": "mistral-moderation-2603",
      "input": ["text to moderate"]
    }'
  ```
  [6]

- **Chat Moderations (multi-turn conversations):**
  ```curl
  curl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/moderations \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $MISTRAL_API_KEY" \
    -d '{
      "model": "mistral-moderation-2603",
      "input": [{"role": "user", "content": "..."}]
    }'
  ```
  [7]

The feature is explicitly designed for detecting harmful or PII (Personally Identifiable Information) content in production environments [1][5].",
