{
  "answer_markdown": "In **Mistral Vibe Code Web**, uncommitted GitHub sandbox files **do not persist** after the session ends [3]. When the session transitions to the **End** phase (due to stopping, timeout, or error), the sandbox is **deleted**, including all uncommitted files [2]. This means you **cannot resume an inactive session**—once the sandbox is deprovisioned, the session is lost [4]. To continue working, you must **start a new session** [3][4].\n\nIf you are using the **CLI**, you can resume a session with:\n```bash\nvibe --continue\n```\nor by specifying a session ID:\n```bash\nvibe --resume SESSION_ID\n```\nHowever, this only works for **active sessions with enabled logging** (`log_interactions = true` in `~/.vibe/config.toml`) [5].",
