Question: I'm building a small tool that lets users pull down files they previously uploaded, and I'm wiring up the download step right now. In Mistral AI's Files API, what parameter does the `GET /v1/files/{file_id}/content` (Download File) operation require, and what does it return on success?

Sources:
[1] https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/files#operation-files_api_routes_download_file
Files API > Download File
Files API > Download File

## Download File {#operation-files_api_routes_download_file}

`GET /v1/files/{file_id}/content`

Download a file

- Operation id: `files_api_routes_download_file`
- Tag: files



[2] https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/files#operation-files_api_routes_get_signed_url
Files API > Get Signed Url > Parameters
Files API > Get Signed Url > Parameters

### Parameters

- `file_id` (string (uuid), required, in path)
- `expiry` (integer, optional, in query) — Number of hours before the URL becomes invalid. Defaults to 24h. Must be between 1h and 168h.



[3] https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/batch-processing#get-batch-job-results
